{"name":"Dull Dusky Pink","hex":"#8f6d73","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dull","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Lacking the ability to cut easily; not sharp.","Boring; not exciting or interesting."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To render dull; to remove or blunt an edge or something that was sharp.","To soften, moderate or blunt; to make dull, stupid, or sluggish; to stupefy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dull"},{"term":"dusky","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Dimly lit, as at dusk (evening).","Having a shade of color that is rather dark."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dusky shark.","A dusky dolphin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dusky"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dusky","blocks":[{"text":"Dusky is an English electronic music duo from London consisting of Alfie Granger-Howell and Nick Harriman. Formed in 2011, they have released music on various records labels, before setting up their own label 17 Steps in July 2014 with the release of the Love Taking Over EP."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dusky"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.o